{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO","title":"ColoringStrategy","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Coloring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/Coloring.swift#L109"},"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast"],"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ColoringModule/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"abstract":[],"title":"ColoringModule","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"ColoringStrategy","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/saturationLargestFirst":{"abstract":[{"text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a vertex of greatest degree, then repeatedly the uncoloured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with the most distinct colours among its neighbours, ties to the greatest degree in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole graph, then to the lesser index. Exact on bipartite graphs. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.saturationLargestFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/saturationlargestfirst","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saturationLargestFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/Equatable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/equatable-implementations","abstract":[],"title":"Equatable Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/connectedSequentialDepthFirst":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same in depth-first preorder. O(n + m)."}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.connectedSequentialDepthFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/connectedsequentialdepthfirst","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"connectedSequentialDepthFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/coloredNeighbors":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/coloredneighbors","abstract":[{"text":"First the vertex of greatest degree (the least index on ties), then repeatedly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uncoloured vertex with the most coloured neighbours. Ties among those fall as a two-way","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indexed binary max-heap breaks them, not by index: vertices are pushed in index order and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raised neighbour by neighbour in ascending order; an entry moves above an equal parent and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sinks to the left child unless the right one is strictly greater. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.coloredNeighbors","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"coloredNeighbors"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","title":"ColoringStrategy.connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Components by least vertex, each in breadth-first order from its least vertex, neighbours in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/connectedsequentialbreadthfirst"},"doc://ColoringModule/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP"},"doc://ColoringModule/s12CaseIterableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.CaseIterable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s12CaseIterableP"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/largestFirst":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Degree descending, the lesser index first on ties: Welsh–Powell, which colours class by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class in this order and gives the same colouring as first fit. O(n + m)."}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.largestFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/largestfirst","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"largestFirst"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/independentSet":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/independentset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Colour classes one at a time: class k is a maximal independent set of the vertices not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coloured, built by repeatedly taking the one with the fewest neighbours among those still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available (the least index on ties) and making it and its neighbours unavailable."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(χ (n + m) log n) for χ classes."}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.independentSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"independentSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/smallestLast":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/smallestlast","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Matula–Beck: repeatedly remove a vertex of least degree in what is left (the least index on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties), then colour in the reverse of that removal order. At most degeneracy + 1 colours, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at most 6 on a planar graph. O((n + m) log n)."}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.smallestLast","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallestLast","kind":"identifier"}]}}}